# Teaching Creating Apps for Devices

<img src="https://images.code.org/77c51c63b972d81ad9defdbd5f2d1769-mb1.png" alt="Image of a microbit" style="border-radius:0px; float: right; height: 275px; clear: both; margin: 0 20px 20px 0;">

Welcome! This professional learning experience is designed help you prepare to teach Code.org's Creating Apps for Devices unit. </p></div>

### **You will:**

* Get an introduction to Creating Apps for Devices.
* Set up your micro:bit.
* Practice key concepts included in the unit.
* Preview end of chapter projects.
* Consider the role of the teacher in a computer science classroom
<br>

<div style="background-color: #F7F8FA; border-radius: 40px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 10px 10px 10px 10px;"> <p style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 13pt;"> 
<b>NOTE:</b> You will need a micro:bit to complete this professional learning experience. 
</p></div>
<br>

**Suggested time:** 100 minutes

## **Take the Pre-Survey**

Code.org values and is responsive to feedback. Please fill out this short pre-survey to  tell us about who you are and how we can best support you.

